WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.535
-Jude Law.
You look great, buddy!

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.904
-Hello. Welcome to my home.
-Thank you so --

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.138
Oh.
-Welcome.

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:08.007
-I'm in your home. See?
Like it or not.

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:11.077
I always knew I'd get an invite.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.846
-I've got to ask.

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.914
So, all these people
you've been interviewing,

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:16.749
you've sat in their houses.

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:20.453
Are you getting, like,
different sort of insight?

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:23.389
Are people, like, super-relaxed
suddenly and just slipping up?

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:25.791
Or have they got, like,
a glass of wine next to them?

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:27.560
-Yeah, that's happened
a few times, yeah.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.295
A couple times
where they had a --

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:31.097
-We're going to have
peachy moments.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:35.534
-The beard is for -- Are you
filming "Fantastic Beasts" now?

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:37.703
-I just started.
We were meant to start --

00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:39.305
I was meant to start on the day

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.241
I believe London
went into lockdown.

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.542
So we were all prepped,
sets built,

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:46.679
everyone ready to go,
rehearsals done, and --

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.581
-Wow.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:51.617
-We all went into our various
lockdown states.

00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:53.119
And so I've just been waiting.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.821
There were several moments
I kept thinking,

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.922
"Ah, you know, maybe I'll just
shave it off, grow it again."

00:00:56.922 --> 00:01:00.026
But I couldn't go through
the two-week burn, you know?

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.861
-Oh, I know that.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.863
There's that two weeks
where it's just so itchy.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:06.399
-It's awful.
The hairs all grow in.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.735
The hairs all start
just going in.

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:11.003
-I always have a weird
couple red hairs.

00:01:11.003 --> 00:01:12.738
Do you have that or no?

00:01:12.738 --> 00:01:14.007
-I'll tell you what I do have,

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.441
since last time
I played Dumbledore,

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:17.443
I have a lot more gray hair,
that's for sure.

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:19.545
[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:21.480
You know, growing it back, yes.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.416
So then I'm like, "Wow.
They're not going to have to

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.384
put anything in there.
That's all me."

00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:26.853
-That's going to happen.
Yeah. Exactly.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.321
That's going to happen, right?

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:32.192
Well, what have you been doing
with your time at home?

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.260
-I've fallen in love
with my garden.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.263
I've realized how lucky I am
to have a garden.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:40.833
And I spent -- We had
the most beautiful spring.

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:44.136
It was, like, the one blessing
amidst this madness.

00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:48.207
And I've become obsessed
with my wisteria.

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:52.111
So, wisteria, if you don't know,
is a creeping flower and plant.

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:53.446
-Yes. It's beautiful.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:57.183
-And it grows along a railing
in my garden.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:00.086
And I've got a raised garden
above that.

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:01.955
And I sort of had this idea

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:04.390
that I wanted it to go up and
go along this railing, too,

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.425
so I trained down two wires,

00:02:06.425 --> 00:02:10.497
and I literally watched
this thing grow up the wire.

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:14.267
And it now goes up the wire
and is growing along the top.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.970
I'm more obsessed with that
than anything else in my life

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.972
at the moment.
My wife thinks I'm going...

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:20.773
-And it smells beautiful, too.
Wisteria.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.441
-It smells great.

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:25.445
Oh, on top of that,
I had a baby, so there you go.

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:26.779
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:29.315
Bury the lead.
Bury the lead on that one.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:33.119
Congrats, Dad.
-Thank you. Yeah.

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:35.921
-That's awesome.
-It's really wonderful.

00:02:35.921 --> 00:02:39.892
So, we are --
Again, we feel pretty blessed

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:44.530
that we were in a time where we
could, as a family, you know --

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:48.400
Uh, we could just nest...
-Yeah.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:54.107
-...and enjoy each other's
company every day as it came.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:03:00.280
It was an unusual but kind of
enforced, you know, love-in.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.880
-Yeah.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:04.283
You know, I was thinking
about you because everyone

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:06.986
started renting and buying
the movie "Contagion."

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:09.688
It was a movie
about a global pandemic.

00:03:09.688 --> 00:03:11.624
-Yeah.
-It was made years ago.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:15.061
Is it eerie to even think
about doing that movie

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:18.097
now that we're kind of
living it?

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:19.998
-Kind of extraordinary,
isn't it?

00:03:19.998 --> 00:03:23.536
First of all, I found it
a little odd that everyone

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:26.539
went back to watch that in
the middle of the real thing.

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.741
-Yeah.
-It was like -- You're like --

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.509
You just turn on the news.
You don't need to watch it.

00:03:30.509 --> 00:03:32.978
But at the same time, it was --

00:03:32.978 --> 00:03:36.415
Yeah, well, first of all,
I think I wrote immediately

00:03:36.415 --> 00:03:37.917
to Steven Soderbergh

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:42.188
and just said, "You got it.
You were there 10 years ago."

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:47.393
And if I'm honest, I remember
also one of the most --

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:51.664
kind of affecting memories
or experiences on that film

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:57.903
were the -- the doctors and the
virologists who are advising us,

00:03:57.903 --> 00:04:00.372
all of whom were these
extraordinary men,

00:04:00.372 --> 00:04:01.940
and they were all saying to us,

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:04.843
"This is a matter of when,
not if."

00:04:04.843 --> 00:04:07.146
And I remember leaving
the whole experience thinking,

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:08.747
"Oh, yeah, you know --"
Look at me.

00:04:08.747 --> 00:04:11.617
You touch yourself on the face
10,000 times a day.

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:12.952
We don't wash our hands.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:15.254
All of that stuff
was sort of embedded in me.

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:18.524
But, of course,
it slowly percolates away.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:21.160
And as you say,
here we are in it.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:25.764
So it is kind of unusual.
-Yeah. Just bizarre.

00:04:25.764 --> 00:04:29.702
It's just -- The whole thing
is just really bizarre.

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:32.505
Even -- I agree with you,
I was like -- I was guilty.

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:34.540
I actually rented the movie,
as well.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.644
And I go, why -- Maybe I was
looking for hints or answers

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:41.680
of how it's going to end.
-Yeah, that's right.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.149
-I was getting advice --

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:45.451
I was like -- "Oh, yeah.
We're living it, yeah."

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:48.053
The last time
you were on our show,

00:04:48.053 --> 00:04:49.789
we talked about
"The Young Pope."

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:51.624
It was just out on HBO.

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:54.193
You told me this story. We never
got around to telling it.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:55.995
But I would like you to --
Do you remember when

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:59.465
Vice President Joe Biden
visited you on the set?

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:04.070
-He did. He did. We were in --

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:07.072
You know, when --
A few people would come by.

00:05:07.072 --> 00:05:12.278
And I always enjoyed meeting
them dressed as the pope.

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:13.779
I mean, who doesn't, right?

00:05:13.779 --> 00:05:15.147
You walk in --

00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:18.517
Especially when you've got
like 20 cardinals around you

00:05:18.517 --> 00:05:21.387
and the Vatican Guard,

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:23.622
it's pretty big
to be in all white.

00:05:23.622 --> 00:05:27.560
But the day he came, I think
I was shooting in the apartment,

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:31.497
and I was in my pajamas,
so it wasn't quite as effective.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:33.199
What a charming man.

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:35.200
He came with -- his whole
family, if I remember,

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.703
because I remember he had
his grandchildren with him.

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:40.472
And he put me at ease
immediately,

00:05:40.472 --> 00:05:42.642
because he literally -- I think
he said something like,

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.943
"It's okay. I've just
come from the real guy."

00:05:44.943 --> 00:05:47.113
-[ Laughs ]
-And I was like, "Oh."

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:50.149
-"Yeah, I just left
the real pope."

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:54.186
-Yeah. "I met the real deal.
You're just an actor."

00:05:54.186 --> 00:05:56.289
-[ Laughs ] I love that.

00:05:56.289 --> 00:05:59.358
Because -- I'll remember that
story because it's so funny.

00:05:59.358 --> 00:06:01.828
You think, "Oh, he's going to
freak out, man."

00:06:01.828 --> 00:06:03.162
-Yeah.

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:04.963
-It's like being in the Vatican,
in the pope's bedroom.

00:06:04.963 --> 00:06:06.532
And, like, what?
And he's like...

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:08.267
"Yeah. Just came
from the real thing.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.135
Anyway, good to see you, kid.
Keep it up."

00:06:10.135 --> 00:06:12.872
[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:14.473
You know, like, completely --

00:06:14.473 --> 00:06:16.542
-It couldn't have been
more boring.

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:18.711
-What a gentleman.
-Yeah, he's a good man.

